Psychol</source><year>1994</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>709</fpage><lpage>724</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8092614</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0003-066X.49.8.709</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Loewenstein</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name><name><surname>Weber</surname><given-names>EU</given-names></name><name><surname>Hsee</surname><given-names>CK</given-names></name><name><surname>Welch</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Risk as feelings</article-title><source>Psych Bull</source><year>2001</year><volume>127</volume><fpage>267</fpage><lpage>286</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0033-2909.127.2.267</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reyna</surname><given-names>VF</given-names></name><name><surname>Farley</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Risk and rationality in adolescent decision making</article-title><source>Psychol Sci Publ Int</source><year>2006</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>44</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1529-1006.2006.00026.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cabanac</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physiological role of pleasure</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1971</year><volume>173</volume><fpage>1103</fpage><lpage>1107</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5098954</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.173.4002.1103</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cabanac</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pleasure: the common currency</article-title><source>J Theoret Biol</source><year>1992</year><volume>155</volume><fpage>173</fpage><lpage>200</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12240693</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0022-5193(05)80594-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Slovic</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Finucane</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Peters</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>MacGregor</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Gilovich T, Griffin D, Kahneman D</surname></name></person-group><article-title>The affect heuristic</article-title><source>Heuristics and Biases: The Psychology of Intuitive Judgment</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>New York: Cambridge University Press</publisher-name><fpage>397</fpage><lpage>420</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Finucane</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Peters</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Slovic</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Schneider SL, Shanteau J</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Judgment and decision making: The dance of affect and reason</article-title><source>Emerging Perspectives on Decision Research</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>New York: Cambridge University Press</publisher-name><fpage>327</fpage><lpage>364</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>DeSousa</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Rationality of Emotion</source><year>1987</year><publisher-name>Cambridge, Massachussetts: MIT Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mellers</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwartz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ho</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ritov</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Decision affect theory: Emotional reactions to the outcome of risky options</article-title><source>Psychol Sci</source><year>1997</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>423</fpage><lpage>429</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1467-9280.1997.tb00455.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mellers</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Choice and relative pleasure consequences</article-title><source>Psychol Bull</source><year>2000</year><volume>126</volume><fpage>910</fpage><lpage>924</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11107882</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0033-2909.126.6.910</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hicks</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Krull</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Gaiso</surname><given-names>AKD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Positive affect and the experience of meaning in life</article-title><source>J Personal Soc Psychol</source><year>2006</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>179</fpage><lpage>196</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0022-3514.90.1.179</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Price</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name><name><surname>Riley</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Barrell</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Are lived choices based on emotional processes?</article-title><source>Cognit Emot</source><year>2001</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>365</fpage><lpage>379</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/0269993004200150</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cabanac</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>What is emotion?</article-title><source>Behav Proc</source><year>2002</year><volume>60</volume><fpage>69</fpage><lpage>84</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0376-6357(02)00078-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Slovic</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Finucane</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Peters</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>MacGregor</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Risk as analysis and risk as feelings: Some thoughts about affect, reason, risk, and rationality</article-title><source>Risk Anal</source><year>2004</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>311</fpage><lpage>322</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15078302</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.0272-4332.2004.00433.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Griffiths</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name><name><surname>Tenenbaum</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Optimal predictions in everyday cognition</article-title><source>Psychol Sci</source><year>2006</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>767</fpage><lpage>773</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16984293</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1467-9280.2006.01780.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref i